edee, who were partners with Simon. Jesus said to Simon, “Don’t be afraid. From now on you will be catching people…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 1:13","note":"When they had come in, they went up into the upper room where they were staying; that is Peter, John, James, Andrew, Philip, Thomas, Bartholomew, Matthew…","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:7","note":"Then he appeared to James, then to all the apostles,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Galatians 1:19","note":"But of the other apostles I saw no one except James, the Lord’s brother.","source":"web"},{"ref":"James 1:1","note":"James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are in the Dispersion: Greetings.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jude 1:1","note":"Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ, and brother of James, to those who are called, sanctified by God the Father, and kept for Jesus Christ:","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H6005","lemma":"עִמָּנוּאֵל","transliteration":"immanuel","gloss":"Immanuel"}],"senses":[{"id":"G2385H","gloss":"James","relation":"G2385H ="},{"id":"G2385I","gloss":"James","relation":"G2385I ="},{"id":"G2385J","gloss":"James","relation":"G2385J ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}